This is the OusiaOS root filesystem: a real ext2 disk (build/disk.img).

/bin  user programs (loaded by execve straight from these ext2 inodes)
/etc  system config (motd, passwd, ousia.conf -- edits persist!)

Unlike the old initrd/tarfs (a RAM filesystem), everything here lives
in on-disk ext2 structures: superblock, block/inode bitmaps, inode
tables with indirect blocks, and directory entries. Writes survive
reboots -- try:

    echo hi > /hi.txt
    cat /hi.txt
    (Ctrl-A X, then `zig build run` again)
    cat /hi.txt     # still there!

The host can inspect this disk with e2fsprogs:

    debugfs -R "ls -l /" build/disk.img
    e2fsck -fn build/disk.img
